problems.problem:
Let $\mathbb{Q}^+$ and $\mathbb{Z}$ denote the set of positive rationals and the set of integers, respectively. Find all functions $f : \mathbb{Q}^+ \to \mathbb{Z}$ satisfying the following conditions:
(i) $f(1999) = 1$;
(ii) $f(ab) = f(a) + f(b)$ for all $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}^+$;
(iii) $f(a + b) \geq \min\{f(a), f(b)\}$ for all $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}^+$.
